\item \code{.pt} checkpoints are exported with Ultralytics (\verb{format = "onnx", half = TRUE}).
\item \code{.onnx} models are converted with \pkg{onnxconverter_common}. Models with opset
< 17 are upgraded to opset 17, internal \code{Cast} nodes are aligned to FLOAT16,
stale shape information is removed, and the original metadata (classes, stride,
image size, task) is preserved so \code{\link[=yolo_model_details]{yolo_model_details()}} keeps working.
\item Input and output tensors of the FP16 model are FLOAT16. pliman converts the
image to half precision and the predictions back to single precision
automatically, so no change is needed in your code.
\item Required Python packages: \verb{pip install onnx onnxconverter_common}
(plus \code{ultralytics} for \code{.pt} files).
}
